{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom at merge 4f427f22acc2084dc282393318b47ade920ccc5c.\n\nThe roster kind vocabulary now has one name and one owner. RosterRoleIsKind became IsActorKind, named for the vocabulary rather than for either caller, and both clauses of the predicate are documented because the second reads as redundancy: the normalizer derives kind unspecified for any word it does not recognise, so comparing kind alone would let unspecified read back as a defined kind.\n\nThe normalization seam itself is unchanged. It was reviewed, its truth table worked by hand, and proved by mutation before this change went near it.\n\nThree live predecessors at these two paths are codex's — 22744290 at internal/workroom, and 9ba72fe1 and c935129e at internal/app — and I cannot retire them: decideSupersede admits a supersession only from the target's own author or a ratifier, with no exemption for naming a successor. I have retired the four that are mine. Saying so rather than leaving the paths looking settled.","body":{"commit":"4f427f22acc2084dc282393318b47ade920ccc5c","merge":"4f427f22acc2084dc282393318b47ade920ccc5c","path":"internal/workroom"}}